A||N||3||Cozmo||Stoopid distributor alignment question...||||5||
Z||000000||Cozmo||04-24-2001||01:46 PM||||OK, I "moroned out" and didn't mark the dist. position on my 2.8 when I removed it to get the heads redone. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>What is the best way to determine the correct orientation? Find TDC on cyl. #1 compression stroke and set the dist. in so the rotor points at plug wire #1?<P>I hate it when I get excited tearing things apart and don't document my witchcraft...<P>over...<BR><P>------------------<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR><I>Suncoast Fieros</I><BR>'85 silver 2M6 4spd. Targa <B>"Silver Streak"</B><BR>'86 black auto GT <B>"Blackbird"</B><BR>'87 white auto Coupe <B>"The Duke"</B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||04-24-2001||02:55 PM||||Well, <B>now</B> you did it.  Throw that car away.  It's a lost cause.  It'll never run again.  Send pictures, and if I like it, I might be kind enough to buy it from you.  I assume you deliver  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.<P>Enough of that.  And the answer is yes, get cylinder #1 on compression, and fix things so the distributor rotor points at #1 plug wire.  After that, the firing order is 1-2-3-4-5-6.<BR> <BR>||||reg||12
Z||000002||EdsB52||04-24-2001||04:59 PM||||Just an obviously simple interjection that many people get backwards. When you search for #1 TDC compression stroke, don't put it between the valve movement. When the valves move, you are at the end of that cylinders exhaust stroke and at the beginning of the intake stroke, or 360 crankshaft degrees (180 distributor degrees) from where you want to be. Simple concept made complicated? Not trying to condescend, but I can't tell you the number of people I've talked to who screw that up and look elsewhere for the problem. It seems people get excited when they see the valves move and think they've arrived. Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_Freak||04-25-2001||12:02 AM||||I'd just pull the number 1 plug.  Put your finger in and have a friend turn the crank with a ratchet.  Roll it until you feel the pressure build and watch for the timing mark around the degree site.  That's close enough to get you to TDC, Jump the ALDL terminal and set the timing.  Good luck||||reg||1
